From 4f37a9a647330b38f7e6fe3044c69da4f82829e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:46:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(upscale): AMD FSR through the AMD FSR SDK 2.4 runtime

ASTROHYBRID_FSR=1 replaces Astro Bot's temporal upscale pass with AMD FSR, as ASTROHYBRID_DLSS does with
DLSS: same pass, colour, motion vectors, depth pairing and jitter conventions (renderer/fsr.inc, included
by dlss.cpp). The SDK's signed Vulkan runtime (amd_fidelityfx_loader_vk.dll and
amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_vk.dll) is loaded at run time from ASTROHYBRID_FSR_PATH; only headers are used
at build time (KYTY_FFX_SDK_DIR). ASTROHYBRID_FSR_VERSION=auto (default) takes the newest version the
runtime offers for the device (FSR 4.1.2 on Radeon RX 6000/7000/9000, otherwise 3.1.6, then 2.3.4) and falls back
to the next one when a context cannot be created. The context is created for the largest input size seen,
with dynamic resolution on. DLSS wins when both are requested. One "FSR 10s:" line every 10 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
